{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "g-23cae583fd75c7",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1200,
			"height": 189,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Event Model\nWhat khora's events mean: identity from what happened, structure from assertions, coherence from frontiers. From K1 (#18, PR #36).\n\nColours: orange = header and Reading, purple = concepts, green = the example, red = not yet decided, none = Decisions.\n\nRendered 2026-11-22 by agent:claude-opus-5-5",
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-055fe026353d0e",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "The three ideas",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 309,
			"width": 1240,
			"height": 352
		},
		{
			"id": "g-14cee7c940bfd9",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 379,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Things are identified by what happened to them**\nNo one decides in advance what deserves identity. Whatever was asserted has it already, so anything can be referred to, annotated or reasoned about later.\n*[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-82aba7f0373abb",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 379,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**One syntax gives structure, meaning stays open**\nEvery statement is a tuple (identity, attribute, value). Entities, properties, relationships and retractions share it, so surfaces treat them alike. What a tuple means comes from its attribute.\n*[[Assertions are tuples with identity]]*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-12575bc4bf13d5",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 379,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Surfaces agree by reading at the same frontier**\nA frontier is a set of events, closed under their causes. Two surfaces built on the same events show consistent views when they read at the same frontier.\n*[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-9aff7572a798db",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Example: Anna creates a project, Ivan renames it",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 781,
			"width": 2040,
			"height": 304,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-23d7731727cd53",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**1. Anna acts**\nAnna, under her grant, through the projects surface, asks to create a project called Kitchen.\nIt is a request, not yet a fact.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-a4f27dbad2bc3e",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**2. khora accepts: event e**\nThe accepted action becomes event **e**, carrying two tuples:\n`e/0 = (,,)`: a new thing\n`e/1 = (e/0, name, \"Kitchen\")`",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-944907db7c41da",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**3. Identities come from e**\nThe project *is* `e/0`.\nIts name, as a statement, is `e/1`, so it can be annotated or retracted later.\nNo id was invented.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-70174dfa2514f5",
			"x": 1960,
			"y": 851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**4. Ivan renames: event f, caused by e**\nIvan read the project at frontier {e}.\n`f/0 = (e/1, retracted, \"true\")`\n`f/1 = (e/0, name, \"Studio\")`\nBoth land together, or neither.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-1f50d02c7a90be",
			"x": 2360,
			"y": 851,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**5. Surfaces read at frontiers**\nAt {e}: Kitchen. At {f}: Studio.\nA surface that has only taken in {e} answers for {e}, or waits.\nHistory shows who renamed it, and why it is Studio.",
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c1aa49132f5078",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Concepts: meaning first, code second",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 1205,
			"width": 1240,
			"height": 796
		},
		{
			"id": "g-a672491fc8eec0",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1275,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event**: something that happened, kept forever with what caused it.\nWhy: the log holds only events; identity and history come from them.\n*In code: `Event`, an envelope around a `Body`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-45844101ff61f8",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 1275,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Accepted action**: one kind of event. A principal asked, khora accepted.\nWhy: a request already says what should be true; no separate outcome or effect is needed.\n*In code: `AcceptedAction { by, action }`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-d3eca79dfaf8e4",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 1275,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Assertion**: a statement (identity, attribute, value). `(,,)` brings a new thing into being.\nWhy: one shape for every kind of statement.\n*In code: `Assertion`; an assert carries several.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-75f24120240691",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1509,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Identity**: what a statement or a thing is known by: its event and its place in it, `e/n`.\nWhy: identity without coordination or naming.\n*In code: `Identity`; well-known ones in `Basic`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-e6a595708eb197",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 1509,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Attribute**: itself a thing with identity. It carries the meaning of the tuples that use it: whether a new value replaces or adds, and its type.\n*In code: an `Identity`; definitions are not built yet.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-69418d9006b811",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 1509,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Cause**: what an event came from. For an action, what its principal had read.\nWhy: \"how did this come to be\" (PRD provenance) and the order between events.\n*In code: `causes`; refused when missing.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-772ff2b9e8ebf9",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1767,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Frontier**: a set of events with all their causes, named by its newest events.\nWhy: the point a read happens at, and what surfaces agree on. Two frontiers can be concurrent.\n*In code: `Frontier`, `FrontierCheck`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-a0cc27560c3992",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 1767,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event id**: a salted hash of the event.\nWhy: tamper-evident, and newest events commit to a whole history, which matters between khoras. The salt stops anyone guessing content from an id.\n*In code: `EventId`, canonical `Json`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-9f8ca76fda0499",
			"x": 1560,
			"y": 1767,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Recorded time**: close to wall time, never backwards, always after the causes.\nWhy: past reads \"as of 3 pm\", and order across writers later; little use yet.\n*In code: `Hlc`.*",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-411c155cb6606e",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Decisions it rests on",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 2121,
			"width": 840,
			"height": 556
		},
		{
			"id": "g-533a898ae41fdb",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2191,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An accepted action is one kind of event]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-1d4f031a1fa928",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2191,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Assertions are tuples with identity]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c7f1e3a8119e81",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2353,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An event carries several assertions]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2b441e8b0741c5",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2353,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Event ids are salted hashes of canonical JSON]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2216eff4c331d7",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2515,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An assert's id is the identity of what it asserts]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2cda1b0c2c1d78",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2515,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 98,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]**\n*design · from the Issue #21 run*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c33964c4314ac4",
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 2121,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Reading · 2026-11-22**\n- The model is built and tested in K1; nothing reads assertions yet. The meaning pays off once a surface does (K6, B2).\n- Attributes carry meaning, but attribute definitions do not exist yet, so a rename relies on an explicit retraction.",
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-8203949e9e7e79",
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 2379,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 290,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Not yet decided**\n- What other kinds of event there are, beyond accepted actions.\n- Whether each log starts with one genesis event.\n- What partial tuples, such as `(p, name, —)`, mean.\n- How rejected requests are kept.\n- How a surface's own events translate into tuples, and back.",
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "spec",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 549,
			"color": "6",
			"text": "## Spec · Event Model\n\n**Purpose:** show what khora's event model *means*, as built in [[Issue #18 Event types ids and clock]] (K1): how things get identity, how structure is asserted, and how surfaces stay coherent.\n\n**Show:** the three ideas; a worked example of people acting over time; each concept with its meaning, why it exists and how it is used, with its code name second; the Decisions it rests on; what is not yet decided.\n\n**Context:** the run's Design section and its Decisions; [[Events are the basic unit of khora]]; the code in `src/kernel/.../event` only to check the canvas matches it.\n\n**Judgement:** meaning before mechanics. Every claim traces to a Decision. Mark what is provisional or open.\n\n**Layout:** row 1 the ideas; row 2 the example; row 3 the concepts; row 4 Decisions and the Reading.\n\n**Triggers:** re-render when the run's Decisions change.\n\n*Draft spec by agent:claude-opus-5-5, to be agreed with a team member.*"
		}
	],
